1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From his cousins, Johannes Praetorius notebook:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1645: Mortensdag (11. nov.) blev herredsfoged Hans Nissen til Hajstrup begravet. (oversat) /Johannes maternal cousin/ 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.fasg.org/Historic.pdf (The Genealogist 14:2000 pp. 159-63): HANS NISSEN, of Hajstrupgård, Vrågård, and Store Tønde, d. Store Tønde, Burkal parish, 11 Nov. 1645, magistrate of Slogs district 1616–45; m. METTA NISDATTER, 
2 CONC d. Store Tønde 3 July 1667, dau. of Nis Asmussen, magistrate of Vis districtSchmidt [supra note 1], 127-29, 160c-60d 196-97, 199. Hans Nissen was granted by the duke of Slesvig the right to hunt hares and foxes with tracking hound
2 CONC s (Friis [supra note 4], 241). For Nis Asmussen’s family, see Gunnar Brun Nissen and Harald Nissen, Slekten Nissen fra Bov Sogn i Sønderjylland (Trondheim,1978). Nis Asmussen’s mother’s father’s father, Jes Thomsen, was ennobled b
2 CONC y King Hans of Denmark in 1488 (Schmidt [supra note 1], 195-96, 216-17; Danmarks Adels Aarbog 25 [1908]: xi-xiii, 78-79). /added by Ella Johansson 10-08-10
2 CONT
2 CONT Ejer af Hajstrupgård og Grøngård. herredsfoged over Schluxharde. Det lykkedes ham at styre den store familiebesiddelse gennem 30 års-krigens forvirring. Sandsynligvis er gården Vrågård skilt ud fra den øvrige bedrift i disse år og
2 CONC  overtaget af den yngre bror Henrich Nissen.
2 CONT
2 CONT
