2 CONT *
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Wikipedia Biographical Summary:==
2 CONT
2 CONT "...'''Johan Christian Fabricius''' (7 January 1745 – 3 March 1808) was a Danish zoologist, specialising in "Insecta", which at that time included all arthropods: insects, arachnids, crustaceans and others. He was a student of Car
2 CONC l Linnaeus, and is considered one of the most important entomologists of the 18th century, having named nearly 10,000 species of animal, and established the basis for modern insect classification..."
2 CONT
2 CONT >''SOURCE'': http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johan_Christian_Fabricius
