1 OCCU Ansat i Borneo-Kompagniet i England, bosat sidst i London
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Forfatter til "Pioneering in the Far East", London 1882. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.saxo.com/dk/pioneering-in-the-far-east-and-journeys-to-california-in-1849-and-to-the-white-sea-in-1878-with-illustrations-etc_ludvig-verner-helms_haeftet_9781241497217
2 CONT
2 CONT *
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilde/Source: Wikipeida: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ludvig_Verner_Helms:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ludvig Verner Helms (1825 – 1918) was a trader and merchant associated with the Far East, especially the Borneo Company in Sarawak.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Varde, Denmark, he left for Bali in 1846, sailing via the Cape and Singapore. He had letters of introduction to Mads Lange and worked for him until 1849. He went briefly to China, then to California in 1850, but ended up t
2 CONC aking up an offer from some Singapore merchants to trade on their behalf in Sarawak, after a mission to Siam and Cambodia.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1851 he took up residence in Sarawak and commenced trading mainly in antimony. In 1856, the Borneo Company was formed and Helms was engaged as its manager in Sarawak. During the Chinese Insurrection against Rajah Brooke in 1857
2 CONC , the insurgents proposed making Helms Rajah, but he was instrumental in their defeat. In 1858, he left for the UK, via Bali, to recover his health and negotiate better terms with the Borneo Company's directors in the UK. In Londo
2 CONC n, in 1859, he married, and engaged to return to Sarawak for the Borneo Company in 1860. He and a growing family stayed until 1872, when they returned to Europe via China, Japan, and California. A lawsuit terminated his relationsh
2 CONC ip with the Borneo Company.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1878, he had a trip to Lapland to investigate mines from the White Sea.
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1881, the family was settled in London,[3] where he stayed until he died in Hampstead in 1918.
2 CONT
2 CONT *
