1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *
2 CONT https://finnholbek.dk/getperson.php?personID=I25210&tree=2
2 CONT **
2 CONT ''Carsten Rickertsen, Sr.''' Mayor of Flensburg, Germany
2 CONT
2 CONT Probably born around 1490 and belonged to one of the 16 century's most famous merchant families in Flensburg, where he even around 1521 may have established himself as a merchant, as he this year occurred in there verified Our Lad
2 CONC y Merchant Guild, or as it was then called,> which broderschup unzer leuen Vrouw des Köpmannens two Flensburger Borch <. In Enemark's> Studies of Customs Accounting material into the 16th Century <, II, page 193, he is mentioned a
2 CONC nd his father as> dedicated horse dealers of the grand style, 'but which also calls traded with oxen, cloth and grain, etc. One of his many prominent trade relations was proconsul in Copenhagen, Henrik Gøye that under Christian II
2 CONC .'s Trip abroad had entrusted the defense of Copenhagen against Frederick I. 's Army (4).
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Knud Gether: Middle-class families in Flensburg and Friesland and their descendants in Denmark, Germany and Norway. 2 volumes. (Lyngby 1986/87), p. 170
2 CONT
2 CONT ATTENTION: "pedigree charts for famous ...." indicates the 1476th birth He was Mayor of Flensburg from approx. 1544 until his death in 154 6
2 CONT
2 CONT Halling bd.1, p.70, Person 17
2 CONT
2 CONT He was "decidedly horse trading by the big size (like his father before him), but acted dusuden with oxen, cloth and grain." One of his many prominent trade relations was proconsul in Copenhagen, Henrik Gøye that under Christian I
2 CONC I's trip abroad had entrusted the defense of Copenhagen against Frederick's army. He belonged to one of the 16 century's most famous merchant families in Flensburg. He had 8 children with Marine Frese. They led all the paysenske w
2 CONC eapons. Family Pays (also stavwet Pais) was one of the late Middle Ages most famous noble families in North Frisia. Its weapon was a right-facing armor-clad arm with a drawn sword in his hand, and equally on the helmet.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Carl Muller: Born in 1490-year. As the danger kjøpmann in Flensburg. Brunettes Every mayor in the same place. (Brunettes 1542). 3 sons and 4 daughters in ekteskapet, Gether informed the conference 8 child. (Halling bd.1, p.70
2 CONC , Person No. 17, also p. 262) All the eight the children led the paysenske våpen. (Source: Knud Gether: Medieval Families from Flensburg, Danish Historical Handbook Publishers, 1986-87) bd.1, p. 170, personal A.32 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Knud Gether: Medieval Families in Flesborg and Friesland and their
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Die Flensburger Family Rickertsen im 16th Jahrhundert RC. Bibl. Peter Tramsen
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Eyvind Andersen Christensen Gedcomp file 10111a 15th January 1998
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) Data from Georg Agerby, Gildhøj 86, DK-2605 Brøndshøj
2 CONT
2 CONT 5) Per Engel Jonasen: Main Road 56 b, 2600 Glostrup, Gedcomp 01230d 2/5-2000
2 CONT
2 CONT 6) January Dambaek, OMV AG, Lassallestraße 3, A-1020 Vienna, Jan.Dambaek @ omv.com 
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference: [http://www.adelby.com/html/p000397.htm#P718/ Carsten Rickertsen, Sr.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Carsten Rickertsen''' (1490-1546)
2 CONT
2 CONT Großvater väterlicherseits des Vor-Vorgängers: Bürgermeister in Flensburg, St. Marien
2 CONT * 1490 in Flensburg † 1546 in Flensburg Vater: Rickert Haysen Mutter: Inge Richarts oo ... mit Metta (Marine) Frese, * 1495 in Emmelsbüll b. Emmelsbüll-Horsbüll, † 15.09.1570 in Flensburg. Lebensphasen: Beruf:	seit um 1543 bis 154
2 CONC 6 Bürgermeister in Flensburg, St. Marien. St. Marien Beruf:	Kaufmann in Flensburg Notizen zur Person: Flensburg. Bürgermeister in Flensburg. Er erbte das Haus, heute Große Str. 48 nach seinem Vater Kinder: 1) Peter Rickertsen, Rat
2 CONC sherr in Flensburg
2 CONT * (s) 1525, † 19.08.1593 in Flensburg oo ... mit Marine Peters.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Ingeborg Rickertsen
