1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Porträtt: Johannes PRÆTORIUS (1750–1826), plantation owner; & pendant: spouse, [née Maren Marie Elisabeth Bröchner (1752–1821)], pstl, 33x25.4 (Copenhagen, Bredgade, Bruun Rasmussen, 12.XI.1986, Lot 64, DKr30,000)
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes Prætorius was born in Skærbæk Sogn, Tønder Amt, Denmark on about 30 March 1750.  	He was married on 15 October 1776 to Maren [Maria] Elisabeth  Brøchner,* born in Randers, Denmark in 1752.     	In February 1777, he was re
2 CONC cognized as an Managing Clerk [Fuldmægtig] in Christiansted.   	On 11 April 1780, he was recognized as an Attorney in the Danish West Indies.   In December 1784, he and his family which consisted of himself, his wife, two boys and
2 CONC  3 girls, were living at 17 Company Street, Christiansted, which belonged to Christopher MacEvoy.   	In 1785-87, he was a [Royal ] Bookkeeper on St. Croix.  	On 31 July 1786, he was made a member of the government with the duty of
2 CONC  being Bookkeeper for the Dutch Loan.   	She died on 23 July 1821 in Rendsborg, Denmark.   	He died on 2 March 1826 in Copenhagen, Denmark.  
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Child of Johannes and Maren Elisabeth Prætorius: 
