0 @N6000000004533559446@ NOTE e-mail from Niels Høyvald <niels@blast.net> Nov 13, 1997.
1 CONT Notes for Carsten Rickertsen:
1 CONT He was just like his father a merchant in Flensburg and Mayor of thecity. It is estimated that he was born in or about 1490.
1 CONT He entered the merchant or Liebe Frauen Guild in 1521.
1 CONT He is entered as Karsten Richquarson in 1521. His house was situatedin Suedermarkt from Angelthor the 25th or the next last before Rude orRoten Street.
1 CONT In the author Enemarks studies he is mentioned on page 193 vol 2 asone of the great horse traders of the time and he did also business inoxen, cloth, grain, etc.
1 CONT He must already have had important trade relations with the greatsupporter of the King Christian the 2nd, namely Knight Henrik Gjoe theManager of the city of Copenhagen in the year 1527. He had then leftCopenhagen (Henrik Gjoe) an
1 CONC d settled in Bremen where he had createdquite a lot of debts for the support of his waiters and horses, hethen made peace with King Frederik the 1st  in May 1525 and returnedto Denmark where he was given the city of Vordingborg as
1 CONC  income.
1 CONT In the meantime a Bremen man by the name of Kort Kreye had imprisonedtwo of Carsten Rickertsens waiters in Germany taken there tradinggoods and now he wanted only to release these if the debt was paid.
1 CONT Carsten Rickertsen complained to the King who wrote the Mayor and citycouncil in Bremen on his behalf... a long letter in old German.
1 CONT After having had several honoree positions in Flensburg it isistimated that he became Mayor in about 1542.
1 CONT His name as Mayor appears on the estate of Janssen and Frau Phalech inOctober 1545.
1 CONT He died in 1546 and after his death a battle over debt for horsestraded with some Swiss came up and a note of the settlement in 1547exist, also his widow Marine fought over a right away by her house andwon in May 1553.
0 @N6000000003304759799@ NOTE begyndt dom bogholder ved det guineiske kompagni, senere selvst. grosserer og
1 CONT skibsreder, 1802 Ældste i grosserersocietetet. 1812 etatsraad.
1 CONT Kobberstik findes på Rigsarkivet. 9299.
1 CONT
1 CONT Children
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Has No Children Elisabeth Prætorius b: 6 DEC 1774
1 CONT    2. Has Children Sophie Frederikke Prætorius b: 8 MAY 1777 c: 16 MAY 1777 in Garnisions K., Kbh.
1 CONT    3. Has No Children Gjertrud Dorothea Prætorius b: 9 JUN 1779 in Kbh. c: 17 JUN 1779 in Garnisions K., Kbh.
